 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/De9hAQGhuvM/",
 "title": "You don't have the power to ruin my day",
 "topic": "mindset",
 "summary": "Ryan Leak shares a story about ordering airport food where a worker wanted to charge 75 cents for barbecue sauce. Instead of matching negative energy, Ryan tipped the worker $10, teaching that you set the standard for your day and should be generous regardless of others' attitudes.",
 "key_points": [
  "The creator was at an airport eating mediocre chicken tenders and asked for a side of barbecue sauce after paying for food.",
  "The waiter said it would cost 75 cents, prompting the creator to point out the hassle of swiping a card, signing slips, and leaving a tip for sauce.",
  "The creator accepted the cost, paid, and then left the waiter a $10 tip.",
  "After the tip, the waiter's attitude changed and he tried to bring better service.",
  "The creator states the reason for doing this was not to brag about having $10, but to show the waiter he did not have the power to ruin the creator's day.",
  "The creator explains: I don't match the energy, I set the standard.",
  "The creator notes the waiter did not deserve a big tip for mediocre barbecue sauce, but the creator is called to be generous because he received an unearned eternal jackpot.",
  "The podcast host concludes that people only have the power to upset you if you hand them the keys to your heart."
 ],
 "content": "You don’t have the power to ruin my day. the other day, i was at an airport eating some mediocre chicken tenders and i went to this restaurant and i had forgotten to get like some barbecue sauce and i had already paid for my food. and i said hey can i get a side of barbecue sauce? and this waiter he goes it'll be 75 cents. i said dude really? so you want me to pull out my credit card and you're going to swipe it and you're going to give me two slips, one for the merchant, one for the customer and then and then now i have to leave you a tip, right? and and i can tell he was trying to make the point. and i said okay, you make your point i'll make mine. all right. so that's mine. so he gives me mediocre barbecue sauce with the mediocre chicken tenders and and then i left him a $10 tip. and then his attitude changed real fast. now he's like trying to bring me premium chicken tenders. you know what i'm saying? i'm like oh these are in the back who are these for, you know? and the reason i did that isn't to just say y'all balling because you know i got $10. and um but the reason i did it is because i i just wanted him to know you don't get to ruin my day. no no no i don't match the energy. i set the standard. i'm going to have a great day. why? you you don't deserve that kind of tip for barbecue sauce that is mediocre. but God hasn't called me to match mediocre for mediocre. God's called me to be generous. and so it's not about money. it's about carrying a heart that says you know what kind of person I am? I won the eternal jackpot. I got something that I did not deserve. and because I got something that I did not deserve, well it makes me want to give away to people what they don't deserve. THE MINIMALISTS • EPISODE 561 interesting about this to me is you don't have the power to upset me unless I hand you the keys to my heart.",
